Myth: In the wake of the great stillness, the architects of the firmament contemplated the nature of the void. They saw that silence, if left to fester, became a fortress of isolation, hardening around the heart like frozen starlight. Yet, they discovered that the stone of this fortress was not impenetrable; it was, in truth, brittle. To break the silence was not merely to act, but to perform a sacred geometry of reconciliation.

Lyra, in her wisdom, understood that the bridge between her and Boreas had not collapsed, but had simply lost its frequency. To restore the Resonant Chord, she chose to cast her light inward, gathering the fragments of her previous efforts into a singular, glowing sphere. She did not cast this light to demand a return, but to illuminate the path for a potential reunion. Her gesture was a quiet defiance against the gravity of the void. As the light expanded, it reached the hidden corners of the firmament, touching the dormant potential within the surrounding dark. Even if the universe offered no immediate reflection, the act of giving remained its own destination, for in the moment of release, the bridge was already reborn, existing in the intention of the giver.

